Chapter: RvFramelessTemp

 The frameless path allocates temporaries by cycling t3, t4, t5, t6 with no
 liveness, so a right operand that allocates FOUR temporaries lands its
 fourth on the register the left operand is still sitting in. Every shape
 below is built to that count: one allocation for the left, four inside the
 right, and the outer instruction then reads its own left operand back as
 something else.

 `rv-frameless-imm` pins the literal-operand half of the same defect, which
 the immediate forms closed by never materialising the right operand at all.
 These are the register forms, where there is a second register to clobber.

Section: Probe

  mix-shl : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mix-shl (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else mix-shl (n - 1) (bit-xor acc (bit-shl (bit-and n 7) (bit-and (bit-shru (bit-xor n 1) 2) 3)))

  mix-and : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mix-and (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else mix-and (n - 1) (acc + bit-and (bit-or n 992) (bit-and (bit-shru (bit-xor n 1) 2) 255))

  mix-add : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mix-add (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else mix-add (n - 1) (acc + (bit-and n 15) * (bit-and (bit-shru (bit-xor n 1) 2) 7))

  mix-sub : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mix-sub (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else mix-sub (n - 1) (acc + ((bit-and n 63) - (bit-and (bit-shru (bit-xor n 3) 1) 15)))

  mix-shru : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mix-shru (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else mix-shru (n - 1) (bit-xor acc (bit-shru (bit-or n 4080) (bit-and (bit-shru (bit-xor n 1) 2) 3)))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (show (mix-shl 12 0))
   print-line-uni (show (mix-and 12 0))
   print-line-uni (show (mix-add 12 0))
   print-line-uni (show (mix-sub 12 0))
   print-line-uni (show (mix-shru 12 0))
  end
